node.doctext:
Why does using $# define a previously undefined variable?

<code>
#!/usr/bin/perl 
$array=undef;
warn "array ",defined($array) ? 'is' : 'is not'," defined";
warn '$#{$array} is ',$#{$array};
warn "array ",defined($array) ? 'is' : 'is not'," defined";
</code>

Produces this:

<code>
array is not defined at /home/smitty/bat/t line 3.
$#{$array} is -1 at /home/smitty/bat/t line 4.
array is defined at /home/smitty/bat/t line 5.
</code>
